## Original Content
<p>I'm excited to share that Coursera is making a $100 million strategic investment in LearnVector Inc., a newly formed AI-native learning company founded and led by Andrew Ng — one of the world's most influential figures in AI. </p>
<p>The post <a href="https://blog.coursera.org/coursera-invests-in-learnvector-to-build-the-future-of-ai-native-learning/">Coursera invests in LearnVector to build the future of AI-native learning</a> appeared first on <a href="https://blog.coursera.org">Coursera Blog</a>.</p>

## Summary
Coursera has made a $100 million strategic investment in LearnVector Inc., an AI-native learning company founded by Andrew Ng. The investment aims to advance AI-native learning technologies and build future platforms. This partnership underscores the increasing integration of AI in educational sectors.

## Key Points
- Coursera invests $100 million in LearnVector Inc.
- LearnVector Inc. is a newly formed AI-native learning company
- Andrew Ng, a renowned AI expert, founded and leads LearnVector Inc.
- The collaboration focuses on developing AI-native learning solutions


